/**
 * \mainpage StEventMaker — Maker that creates and registers the StEvent object
 *
 * \section evtmkr_purpose Purpose
 * StEventMaker is the gateway maker that creates a fresh \c StEvent instance
 * at the start of every event and posts it to the StChain whiteboard under
 * the key \c "StEvent".  All downstream makers retrieve the event object via
 * \c GetStEvent() or \c GetInputDS("StEvent").  Without StEventMaker running
 * first, no other maker can store or retrieve event data.
 *
 * In legacy production mode, StEventMaker can also load pre-formed hit
 * collections from a DST dataset and attach them to StEvent.  Boolean flags
 * on the maker instance control which collections are loaded
 * (\c doLoadTpcHits, \c doLoadFtpcHits, \c doLoadSvtHits, \c doLoadSsdHits,
 * \c doLoadTptTracks, \c doLoadEstTracks).
 *
 * \section evtmkr_input Input
 * - Optional DST dataset (\c GetDataSet("dst")) for legacy hit loading.
 * - \c StDetectorDbBeamInfo database table for StRunInfo population.
 *
 * \section evtmkr_output Output
 * - A new \b StEvent instance registered on the StChain whiteboard under
 *   the key \c "StEvent", with \c StRunInfo populated.
 *
 * \section evtmkr_classes Key Classes
 * | Class | Role |
 * |-------|------|
 * | StEventMaker | Creates and registers StEvent each event |
 * | StEvent | Central event data store for the STAR framework |
 * | StRunInfo | Run-level metadata (beam energy, species, etc.) |
 * | StEventManager | Abstract interface for event management |
 * | StRootEventManager | ROOT-based implementation of StEventManager |
 *
 * \section evtmkr_usage Usage Example
 * \code{.cpp}
 * // StEventMaker should be the first maker in the chain:
 * StEventMaker* evtMaker = new StEventMaker("StEventMaker", "StEventMaker");
 * chain->AddMaker(evtMaker);
 *
 * // Downstream maker retrieves StEvent:
 * StEvent* event = (StEvent*) GetInputDS("StEvent");
 * \endcode
 *
 * \note StEventMaker must be the first (or one of the first) makers in any
 *       reconstruction or analysis chain so that StEvent exists before any
 *       maker tries to fill or read it.
 */
